    {
      "id": "format.pages_allocation_usage",
      "implementation": "implemented",
      "verification": "internal_only",
      "required_verification": "dao_differential",
      "reason": "Bounded complete-page reads, allocation-free sequential streaming, SRC-0020 detached usage-map primitives, and EXP-0057 table-owned page traversal are implemented. From a caller-supplied table-definition root, the reader locates and delimits the owned-map row, handles inline maps, treats a zero type-1 slot as null, follows a bounded prefix of direct checked type-05 page references, and derives extended pages from the checked slot-relative base. Traversal rejects malformed row directories and flags, out-of-capture references, self-references, repeated pages, nonzero slots after null, arithmetic overflow, and resource exhaustion with fixed page storage and pre-charged visited state. This does not locate a catalog, discover table roots, establish global allocation state, choose pages for writes, decode row values, or provide DAO differential verification. The implementation and exploratory observations remain internal_only and make no compatibility claim.",
